 "intro": "Jotapata in Galilee, summer 67 AD. You are Vespasian, sent by Nero with three legions to crush the Jewish revolt. Your son Titus is with you. The defender is Joseph ben Matthias, later the historian Josephus.",
 "debrief": "Josephus himself tells the story. Vespasian built a mound against the only approachable side. The defenders hung dripping clothes on the walls to hide their thirst, softened the ram with sacks and poured boiling oil. After 47 days a deserter revealed that the guards slept before dawn, and Titus led the men over the wall. Josephus survived a suicide pact in a cave, surrendered, and foretold that Vespasian would become emperor. The other choices are what-ifs.",
